[{:db/id -1
  :adr/id "ADR-2608151900"
  :adr/title "Bots Goal is a durable AgentRun with host receipts and bounded child runs"
  :adr/status "accepted"
  :adr/date "2026-08-15"
  :adr/body
  "## Decision

The mobile Bots Goal path is detached from its HTTP stream. Submission creates
one persistent `agent.run/AgentRun`; a local three-slot worker pool owns the
execution, so closing the screen does not cancel it. A server restart turns a
running Goal into a checkpoint and re-enqueues it. Ordinary chat remains a
synchronous visible turn.

The Goal provider must first record a dependency-aware plan of one to eight
steps. Tool actions, output digests, bounded duration, child-run identity and
verifier decisions are appended by the host. Provider prose cannot manufacture
an execution receipt. `goal_complete` is admitted only after every plan step
has a host action receipt and has passed the step verifier.

A provider may request up to three independent read-only tools together. Each
becomes a child AgentRun whose `:agent.run/parent` is the Goal run. The host runs
those children concurrently. Unknown, connector-blocked, write, approval, and
Goal-control tools are refused on the parallel path; writes keep the existing
single approval boundary.

## Why

The earlier Goal loop kept an HTTP request open, stored only a visible turn,
relabelled every running turn as interrupted after restart, rejected multiple
tool calls, and accepted model-written evidence as completion. It therefore
looked active while still behaving like a long chat response.

This adapter uses the application's existing AgentRun vocabulary instead of
inventing another scheduler. The visible turn remains the mobile projection;
the AgentRun, plan, child runs and append-only event ledger are the durable
execution truth.

## Bounds

This is process-resident execution, not a claim that work continues while the
Mac is asleep. Parallelism is read-only and capped at three. Coding writes do
not yet receive automatic worktree merge arbitration; they remain serialized
behind the established approval or omakase receipt.

## Verification

Tests prove that submit returns while the provider is blocked, two read actions
finish as sibling child AgentRuns, the plan cannot finish without host receipts,
step and Goal verifiers append receipts, and restart recovery produces a
resumable checkpoint rather than an interrupted terminal."}]
